I think your SP bias is showing again. You've made plenty of points about 
how adding MP can provide a distraction or an unnecessary change, but you 
haven't provided any evidence that I can see that "multiplayering" a game 
diminishes it, which is really what you're saying in this post.

> The changes to balance, the maps, the
> events, etc etc. They were all needed to make the game fair for MP

This makes no sense unless you're willing to say that it's ok for sides to 
be unbalanced when you're playing vs. the computer. And yet people bitch and 
moan about an AI that cheats. Why? Because they want balance and fairness on 
all sides and they want an AI that can play as well as any human. If what 
you're saying is that you like having the option of re-rolling until you get 
enough of an advantage over the AI that you'll be sure to be able to stomp 
it, then ok, I see why you prefer SP and see why you don't care that the 
sides are balanced. But I don't think most good gamers want that, I think 
they'd prefer to have a game that was up to the challenge of beating them, 
and one that plays fair on a level playing field where all options are 
reasonable balanced so that there's no obvious undeatable strategy (like 
playing Black Dragons with Apocalypse in Heroes).

The argument is often made that adding multiplayer is a cheap way of 
avoiding having to put in a good AI. I think the opposite is true. Not 
offering multiplayer is a cheap way of not having to balance. If single 
players don't mind being able to stomp an AI with various killer strategies, 
then it's ok to ship the product that way and not have to go through the 
laborious and challenging task of ensuring that there is no single killer 
strategy and all options are balanced, something you get burned doing if you 
release for MP.

> I sure hope he doesnt hold up MoM2 trying to MP it right off the bat

That's the best reason you've offered to date and one I can completely 
understand.

